1
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:08,590
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:13,325 --> 00:02:42,435
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,120
Once upon a time...

4
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:36,740
... a sparrow...

5
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:41,620
... was yearning for food.

6
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:46,320
Later on...

7
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:49,960
... as the sparrow was desperately
searching for food ...

8
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:53,600
... it was getting closer and closer to
the trap of a hunter.

9
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:58,780
Poor sparrow...

10
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:06,800
...,just as it was about to be trapped,
was noticed by a hawk flying in the sky.

11
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:10,720
The hawk immediately descended...

12
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:15,200
... and caught the sparrow a second
before it went into trap.

13
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:18,339
However...

14
00:04:19,899 --> 00:04:21,760
... later the hawk realized...

15
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:25,240
... it got into trap too.

16
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,420
The hawk then looked the hunter in the
eyes...

17
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,660
... and told him..

18
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:39,980
... ''Please have mercy on me.''

19
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,160
''You have everything you need.''

20
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:50,640
''We don't know each other.''

21
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,820
''I got into your trap reluctantly.''

22
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:58,060
''Just set me free.''

23
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:00,960
''Also''...

24
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:04,260
... ''Never I did something bad to you.''

25
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,540
The hunter...

26
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:14,880
... contemplated for a while...

27
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,420
... and then told the hawk...

28
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:23,220
...''What about the sparrow? Has it ever
done something bad to you?''

29
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:30,340
Then the hunter set the sparrow free...

30
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:35,600
... grabbed the hawk by its feet...

31
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:40,640
... and went on his way to the village.

32
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:48,980
Whether muslim or not...

33
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:56,080
... the sparrows of these lands are
entrusted to us.

34
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:07,160
We will make those inglorious dogs regret
everything they had done.

35
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:12,120
We are going to stick the arrow of justice
on their throats!

36
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:57,240
We have become sick of waiting for you!

37
00:06:57,860 --> 00:07:02,200
So we armed ourselves and came here
to fight side by side with the Valiants.

38
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,600
Welcome.

39
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:06,940
You already brought joy, Hatuns.

40
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:35,700
The soldiers of Yarıhisar are strong
enough to defend their castle.

41
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:37,800
But...

42
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:41,220
... in order to defeat the Turks outside
the castle...

43
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,640
... we need support.

44
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,180
Don't we, Helen?

45
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:47,480
Yes, we do.

46
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:50,720
We need support to defend the Keşiş
Strait.

47
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:56,720
If they move together with the soldiers
of Bilecik's feudal lord...

48
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:59,380
... and fight together...

49
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:02,720
... along with the help of our soldiers...

50
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:07,240
... they will do more than just defending
the Keşiş Strait...

51
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:09,280
... in my opinion.

52
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,420
I will handle this issue, Nikola.

53
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,780
I'd be glad.

54
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:18,980
The door!

55
00:08:58,520 --> 00:08:59,800
Bravo, Nikola!

56
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,200
Bravo.

57
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:10,660
Flatyos.

58
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:12,600
I wasn't expecting this.

59
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,140
Doesn't Osman want the same thing?

60
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:18,020
Killing you when you don't expect him.

61
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:26,620
Our assault shook Osman so bad that I'm
sure he can't find the way of his Tent.

62
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:34,220
Yes. We destroyed his dream of becoming
the Sultan of a state, Nikola.

63
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,920
But you know Osman.

64
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:38,640
He won't give up.

65
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:41,360
We always need to be careful.

66
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:46,420
The suffering of Osman gives me
power, Flatyos.

67
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:50,120
When he suffers, I constantly feel
reborn.

68
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:53,800
And just like you say, he is Osman
after all.

69
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:56,800
I'm sure he is planning his next move
right now.

70
00:09:57,340 --> 00:10:01,820
I'm going to end him the moment he puts
his plan in action.

71
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:06,680
The support our emperor has sent will
arrive here soon.

72
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:11,700
We are going to struck them like a
thunderbolt, Flatyos.

73
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:34,020
It's me, Alexander!

74
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:35,280
Stop!

75
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:36,780
It's me.

76
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:41,780
Alexander, you fool!

77
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:03,100
I see these lands made you stronger,
my friend.

78
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:05,500
And your sense of art didn't soften you.

79
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,620
You fool!

80
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:10,160
Don't you know the crown on my head is
sacred?

81
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:14,040
Whatever we went through happened as to
fools like you!

82
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:29,080
When new one comes, the old one loses its
value, my friend.

83
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:44,940
Our emperor has declared you the new
lord of all feudal lords.

84
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,160
And this is...

85
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,920
... your new crown, my friend.

86
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,340
Congratulations, Nikola.

87
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,840
Where are my troops, Alexander?

88
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:26,240
I came first to make way, my friend.

89
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:30,060
I will bring your troops tomorrow when
it's more secure.

90
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:34,320
Then we will wait for your order to
attack the Turks.

91
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:53,440
Our dreams will soon come true, Mighty
Caesar.

92
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:56,960
So soon.

93
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:31,840
After he saw that child in Söğüt in such
a condition...

94
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:36,860
... he has started burn with the pursue
of revenge.

95
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:42,440
Inshallah, my Rab will grant us victory
soon.

96
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:45,340
Inshallah.

97
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:49,620
Otherwise, we can't cool off the anger
of my Bey.

98
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:16,780
Don't worry, Gonca Hatun.

99
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:21,500
No one can harm you when you are with us.

100
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:39,680
I brought you biscuits.

101
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:45,020
They will give you strength while
fighting.

102
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:50,340
They are for all of us, right?

103
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:14,500
Loony lad, he is.

104
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,980
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

105
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,240
Bon appetit.

106
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:42,640
I heard you haven't had anything for days.

107
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,900
The moment I got in power...

108
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:01,920
... they tried to destroy my reputation.

109
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:08,060
If I don't get my revenge from them...

110
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:12,880
... we might never be taken serious
again, my Bala.

111
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:15,060
You are right, my Osman.

112
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:20,420
But remember that you never left a
misdeed unpunished.

113
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,680
I'm a Bey now.

114
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:28,580
They will enjoy even the smallest misdeed
done against me.

115
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:39,640
I'm sure they are willing to destroy my
reputation before I get stronger.

116
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:46,900
For sure, they know the Valiants of these
lands...

117
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,960
... will become one under the flag of
mine.

118
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:56,480
For this exact reason, they are trying
to take me down, my Bala.

119
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:06,300
I need to take my revenge before it is
too late.

120
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:14,660
They need to be filled with sorrow before
they even start to enjoy their victory.

121
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:18,460
And they must quiver in fear.

122
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:23,180
People must witness our victory first
so that...

123
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:26,700
... they can become one under our flag
as soon as possible.

124
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:31,600
Praise be upon my Valiant!

125
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:36,360
The Mongols destroyed the Seljuks.

126
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:42,760
And those who fled had to move closer
to the borders of Byzantine.

127
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,380
And now the Byzantine is attacking.

128
00:17:46,220 --> 00:17:48,680
We are in between of two separate flames.

129
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:52,200
Maybe...

130
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:55,120
... if no voice becomes hope for our
people...

131
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,980
... if no flag of a new state flies in the
sky...

132
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:05,420
... and if our people lose their hope
in the end...

133
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:11,000
... we might even get disarrayed for good.

134
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:16,540
This is the sole reason of my fight.

135
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:20,020
Because of this, we can never back down.

136
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:28,660
A thousand thanks to my Rab, he made
me the lover of a such Valiant.

137
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:38,300
Thanks to my Rab, I was granted a
gazelle-eyed beauty who share my dreams.

138
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:45,340
He granted me a lover who is willing
suffer for this cause of mine.

139
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:11,380
My Bey.

140
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:13,680
I have news for you.

141
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:20,100
Troops who left Constantinople to help
Nikola will arrive at İnegöl tomorrow.

142
00:19:21,580 --> 00:19:23,140
Oh, praise be!

143
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:28,820
Thanks to my Rab!

144
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:33,900
Allahu Akbar!

145
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:38,140
Let us come with you, Osman Bey.

146
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:43,520
May you go back to Tent and straighten
the affairs there, my Bala.

147
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:45,880
And send our regards to everyone.

148
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:10,200
The Emperor, Andronikos the third, with
this crown he sent...

149
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:16,220
... has declared his commander and
representative, noble Ayos Nikola,...

150
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:19,700
... from Inegol to Jordan, the feudal
landlord of all borders...

151
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:21,700
...in parallel with Turkish lands.

152
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:28,860
May our Holy Father grant many victories
to Ayos Nikola on his holy mission.

153
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:30,360
Amen!

154
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,440
My sacred friends.

155
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:01,640
My mighty soldiers!

156
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:08,020
We are face to face with the strongest
enemy...

157
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:12,320
... the Roman Empire has ever fought
against since its foundation!

158
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:17,400
Because of this reason, we need to stop
fighting with each other...

159
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:21,520
... and defeat our enemy by becoming one!

160
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:28,720
I, the Lord of all feudal landlords,
Ayos Nikola...

161
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:31,880
... will not disappoint our emperor!

162
00:21:32,660 --> 00:21:41,580
And I promise you all that I will send the
Turks back to where they come from!

163
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:50,020
Alexander, leave this castle now...

164
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,280
... and come with the army that will
bring me victory.

165
00:21:54,460 --> 00:21:57,960
Don't worry, Nikola. You will get your
army today.

166
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:06,780
Alexander, Turks are everywhere.

167
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:10,840
Keep your eyes wide open.

168
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,980
I always liked precautions.

169
00:22:15,740 --> 00:22:19,300
They are the ones who need to be careful.

170
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:22,700
Feudal landlord, Nikola.

171
00:22:38,220 --> 00:22:40,540
Your new crown suits you well, Nikola.

172
00:22:41,100 --> 00:22:44,320
It's an honor to fight for you, Great
Commander.

173
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:48,720
The same applies to you, Flatyos.

174
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:02,540
Let me see it.

175
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:05,980
Okay, continue.

176
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:35,400
Thank you, Hatun

177
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:37,140
May you live long.

178
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:39,440
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

179
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:41,500
I'm always happy to help.

180
00:23:53,540 --> 00:23:55,340
I hope it's for good, son.

181
00:23:58,860 --> 00:24:03,020
Do you think it's unfair to work since you
are the son of a Bey?

182
00:24:03,860 --> 00:24:08,100
Don't you forget that we are working for
the future of all Kayıs.

183
00:24:08,240 --> 00:24:11,620
We are building this place so that they
will always...

184
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:14,100
... have a place to educate themselves.

185
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:16,480
Can't you face this fact?

186
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,140
I want to become an Alp and fight.

187
00:24:28,180 --> 00:24:31,600
The world is full of Alps and soldiers.

188
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:37,640
However, the world lacks enlightened
scholars.

189
00:24:39,060 --> 00:24:40,700
Do you know why?

190
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:45,320
Because without scholars, no state
can survive.

191
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:49,700
The future of a state depends on them.

192
00:24:50,300 --> 00:24:54,560
And Kayı Tent needs those scholars
as well.

193
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:59,240
Father. I'm the only one who is aware of
the flame burning inside me.

194
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:01,100
I want to fight!

195
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,820
Uncle Gündüz!

196
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:09,800
Tell me, nephew.

197
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:12,360
Please back me up.

198
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:14,940
Can a muslim be told not to go fighting?

199
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,320
Of course not.

200
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:31,560
But you are still too young.

201
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:33,800
Hear me out for a second.

202
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,500
One needs to train for fighting.

203
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:42,340
And you, my beloved nephew, hold pen
instead of sword.

204
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:07,600
You are mistaken.

205
00:26:09,980 --> 00:26:12,760
I read in the morning, and train at night.

206
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:17,260
Because I'm a Bey of Kayı.

207
00:26:30,120 --> 00:26:32,480
The last thing he said is true, Savcı.

208
00:26:33,620 --> 00:26:35,020
He is a Bey of Kayı.

209
00:26:37,460 --> 00:26:40,040
And he is going to live his own fate.

210
00:26:41,540 --> 00:26:43,780
He wants to be like his uncle Osman.

211
00:26:44,680 --> 00:26:45,920
Oh, my brother.

212
00:26:47,780 --> 00:26:50,220
Which young boy doesn't?

213
00:26:51,940 --> 00:26:53,580
You are right, brother.

214
00:26:54,940 --> 00:26:57,520
He and his Alps are nowhere to be found.

215
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:59,420
They are probably fighting.

216
00:27:00,120 --> 00:27:02,780
-May Allah make their swords sharp.
-Amin

217
00:27:03,020 --> 00:27:05,580
Let's go. We still have lots to do.

218
00:27:06,340 --> 00:27:09,360
Come on, Alps! We need to be faster.

219
00:27:43,420 --> 00:27:45,000
What's up, Master Davud?

220
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:48,220
It feels like you're not forging steel
this time.

221
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:55,580
Enough, Master Davut. For how long this
resentment going to last?

222
00:27:56,940 --> 00:27:58,100
Answer to me.

223
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:02,520
Why did you favor Dündar Bey on the
election?

224
00:28:04,300 --> 00:28:06,180
You shouldn't be surprised.

225
00:28:06,260 --> 00:28:08,960
You know I want peace since the beginning.

226
00:28:09,080 --> 00:28:13,060
Look what happened just because we
wanted to take İnegöl.

227
00:28:21,020 --> 00:28:25,840
You are referring to the shahada of
Beys, İdris Bey.

228
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:30,280
You make insinuations by the blood of
our martyrs.

229
00:28:30,980 --> 00:28:34,200
Know that I won't hesitate to hit you with
this hammer.

230
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:37,120
I belong to this Tent too, Davud Bey.

231
00:28:38,040 --> 00:28:43,900
Of course I'm sad because of our martyrs
and Flatyos' escape.

232
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:47,800
I only wanted have heart-to-heart talk.

233
00:28:49,180 --> 00:28:50,580
I'm offended.

234
00:28:56,760 --> 00:28:59,300
Every blood droplet will be avenged.

235
00:28:59,940 --> 00:29:03,660
Droplet by droplet, we are going to get
our revenge.

236
00:29:04,080 --> 00:29:05,620
Just like this!

237
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:09,560
Just like this!

238
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:12,080
They are all going to be crushed!

239
00:29:19,860 --> 00:29:22,460
Then, will be cooled down like this.

240
00:29:27,980 --> 00:29:31,680
Inshallah.

241
00:29:32,180 --> 00:29:33,500
Inshallah.

242
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,320
Inshallah.

243
00:29:55,840 --> 00:30:00,420
Tell the soldiers to make themselves
presentable, Commander.

244
00:30:01,560 --> 00:30:05,360
We need to look good for the presence of
feudal landlord Nikola.

245
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:07,480
As you order, my commander.

246
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:02,740
It's a trap! Get on your positions!

247
00:31:09,180 --> 00:31:11,100
Defensive formation!

248
00:31:11,100 --> 00:31:12,680
Don't scatter around!

249
00:31:12,680 --> 00:31:14,500
It's a trap! Be careful!

250
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:18,540
Don't leave your positions!

251
00:31:34,380 --> 00:31:35,660
They are up there!

252
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:35,760
Allahu Akbar!

253
00:33:59,960 --> 00:34:01,820
Allahu Akbar!

254
00:34:57,040 --> 00:34:58,760
Allah is eternal!

255
00:40:16,740 --> 00:40:19,260
Allah is eternal!

256
00:40:21,540 --> 00:40:37,800
Allahu Akbar!

257
00:40:37,840 --> 00:40:39,680
Thank you, my Rab.

258
00:40:42,300 --> 00:40:43,420
Thank you.

259
00:41:39,580 --> 00:41:41,360
I wish you ease, Hatuns.

260
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:43,880
Thank you, Selcen Hatun.

261
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:47,620
I hope it's for good, Hazal Hatun.

262
00:41:49,120 --> 00:41:50,200
Indeed, it is.

263
00:41:50,940 --> 00:41:57,060
I have been sewing and cooking non-stop
for days.

264
00:41:58,740 --> 00:42:00,980
I'm as light as a bird now.

265
00:42:01,160 --> 00:42:03,100
Oh, how magnificent.

266
00:42:04,560 --> 00:42:06,860
But, can you elaborate more?

267
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:15,420
I'm doing these things to take my mind
off Dündar Bey.

268
00:42:17,580 --> 00:42:20,080
You have every right to do these things.

269
00:42:20,740 --> 00:42:23,100
Let Dündar worry about his own-self.

270
00:42:26,240 --> 00:42:27,920
That's what I will do now.

271
00:42:38,400 --> 00:42:40,140
Welcome, my daughter.

272
00:42:40,980 --> 00:42:42,700
Thank you, Selcen mother.

273
00:42:44,160 --> 00:42:45,780
Welcome, Bala Hatun.

274
00:42:46,120 --> 00:42:47,660
Thank you, Hazal Hatun.

275
00:42:47,840 --> 00:42:49,620
-I wish you ease.
-Thank you.

276
00:42:51,700 --> 00:42:53,760
I have things to tell you.

277
00:42:53,860 --> 00:42:55,620
-Follow me.
-Let's go.

278
00:43:05,160 --> 00:43:06,700
I wish you ease, Hatuns.

279
00:43:06,780 --> 00:43:09,620
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

280
00:43:09,640 --> 00:43:12,040
May your hands don't see any trouble.

281
00:43:12,380 --> 00:43:13,880
After you.

282
00:43:35,740 --> 00:43:39,860
Now that Lena Hatun is here, I can start.

283
00:43:40,840 --> 00:43:43,280
Hazal and Lena Hatun.

284
00:43:44,080 --> 00:43:48,500
Teachers are going to be here soon to
teach our children how to read.

285
00:43:50,720 --> 00:43:54,180
Hazal Hatun, I want you to fabricate the
tents.

286
00:43:55,960 --> 00:44:01,680
And Lena Hatun, I want you to provide the
essential goods for them.

287
00:44:03,320 --> 00:44:05,260
These are your duties.

288
00:44:05,360 --> 00:44:06,500
Sure thing.

289
00:44:07,460 --> 00:44:09,360
Sure thing, Bala Hatun.

290
00:44:10,860 --> 00:44:15,440
No one but me can help you with these
things.

291
00:44:18,000 --> 00:44:19,640
Don't worry, Bala Hatun.

292
00:44:21,900 --> 00:44:25,080
I already made the preparations.

293
00:44:26,820 --> 00:44:31,320
Perhaps, you can help us with installing
and furnishing the tents.

294
00:44:32,260 --> 00:44:33,640
Of course.

295
00:44:49,760 --> 00:44:53,720
From now on, only a single Hatun will be
responsible of the drinks.

296
00:44:53,720 --> 00:44:57,460
And who she is shall not make anyone get
close to them.

297
00:44:58,280 --> 00:44:59,860
As you order, Bala Hatun.

298
00:45:09,260 --> 00:45:10,480
I need to go now.

299
00:45:19,860 --> 00:45:22,960
-I wish you ease, Hatuns.
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

300
00:45:23,740 --> 00:45:25,360
May everything be easy.

301
00:45:39,760 --> 00:45:45,440
Now that her little tongue is used to
giving orders...

302
00:45:47,700 --> 00:45:52,760
... may Allah help us from now on.

303
00:45:59,760 --> 00:46:05,200
If it wasn't for your treason, we wouldn't
be hearing her orders.

304
00:46:33,600 --> 00:46:35,360
Selamun Aleyküm.

305
00:46:37,760 --> 00:46:39,760
Aleyküm Selam.

306
00:46:42,160 --> 00:46:43,980
Welcome, Dündar Bey.

307
00:46:44,740 --> 00:46:47,220
-To what do we owe the honor?
-Thank you.

308
00:46:48,080 --> 00:46:49,680
I came to celebrate you.

309
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:52,000
Thanks for coming.

310
00:46:52,300 --> 00:46:53,640
How is the business?

311
00:46:54,460 --> 00:46:55,780
Is everything okay?

312
00:46:56,420 --> 00:47:02,020
Thanks to Osman Bey, we managed to find
a workshop so quickly.

313
00:47:03,760 --> 00:47:06,380
May you be worthy of him.

314
00:47:08,360 --> 00:47:10,680
I see lots of goods.

315
00:47:10,880 --> 00:47:17,000
It's not so easy to bring goods all the
way from Aleppo to here as to Mongols.

316
00:47:17,820 --> 00:47:21,620
There is always a key that can open all
doors.

317
00:47:23,720 --> 00:47:27,480
Do you mean being a successful merchant?

318
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:29,700
I appreciate it.

319
00:47:31,820 --> 00:47:36,900
We also heard about you being an expert
merchant, my Bey.

320
00:47:39,260 --> 00:47:42,580
I was once a merchant but now-

321
00:47:42,620 --> 00:47:45,820
It's easy to be the wolf of mountains.

322
00:47:46,440 --> 00:47:52,260
However, I can't tell the same thing about
being the wolf of trade.

323
00:47:54,120 --> 00:47:58,560
No one is better than you when it comes
to commerce.

324
00:48:00,680 --> 00:48:06,360
And it'd be an honor to make business with
you.

325
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:11,600
Thank you.

326
00:48:12,860 --> 00:48:16,320
You have a smart assistant, merchant
Melih.

327
00:48:19,200 --> 00:48:22,260
Not everyone can find an assistant like
him.

328
00:48:22,860 --> 00:48:24,620
Süleyman is like a son to me.

329
00:48:26,380 --> 00:48:32,940
Dündar Bey, I have been waiting for you to
talk about an opportunity.

330
00:48:33,880 --> 00:48:35,500
I'm listening.

331
00:48:35,640 --> 00:48:38,700
My caravan from Konya will arrive
here soon.

332
00:48:39,500 --> 00:48:44,620
If I can sell the goods that I bought from
the Indian lands in Byzantine cities...

333
00:48:45,140 --> 00:48:46,960
... I will make a huge profit.

334
00:48:48,280 --> 00:48:52,180
And you need a partner who you can trust.

335
00:48:53,340 --> 00:48:54,840
You are right.

336
00:48:54,880 --> 00:48:59,940
Being trustworthy alone is not enough.

337
00:49:01,220 --> 00:49:08,880
We need a Bey who can make peace with
the thereabout feudal landlords.

338
00:49:15,900 --> 00:49:18,000
What's your offer?

339
00:49:18,900 --> 00:49:20,640
Oh, people!

340
00:49:20,920 --> 00:49:22,840
I have news.

341
00:49:24,080 --> 00:49:25,600
I hope it's for good.

342
00:49:25,760 --> 00:49:29,620
People, I have news!

343
00:49:36,100 --> 00:49:39,160
Listen to me carefully, folks.

344
00:49:40,320 --> 00:49:42,340
Open your ears for me.

345
00:49:42,900 --> 00:49:48,840
The revenge of Hasan, İlyas, Fazıl, and
Turan Bey has been taken!

346
00:49:56,940 --> 00:50:02,540
A large army of heathens got ambushed
by Osman Bey near İnegöl...

347
00:50:02,620 --> 00:50:05,480
... and got completely destroyed.

348
00:50:05,800 --> 00:50:13,220
May you live long Osman Bey!

349
00:50:14,080 --> 00:50:18,620
That heathen called Nikola is defeated
once again...

350
00:50:18,680 --> 00:50:22,020
... and the soldiers of Islam are
victorious!

351
00:50:27,660 --> 00:50:32,080
May Allah always help our Osman Bey.

352
00:50:35,320 --> 00:50:41,000
He put a smile on our faces once again.

353
00:50:44,080 --> 00:50:45,520
What's your offer?

354
00:50:47,640 --> 00:50:49,560
Half-and-half, Dündar Bey.

355
00:50:50,940 --> 00:50:52,120
I accept it.

356
00:50:52,420 --> 00:50:54,140
Let's do some business.

357
00:51:07,240 --> 00:51:09,520
Did you see Dündar's face?

358
00:51:12,960 --> 00:51:17,020
I think he didn't like the news.

359
00:51:17,920 --> 00:51:23,300
If you were him, would you like the
victory of your enemy, Simon?

360
00:51:26,160 --> 00:51:29,420
We'll get stronger in the Tent if we
control Dündar.

361
00:51:31,040 --> 00:51:35,200
And we will get the papers we are looking
for in a short time.

362
00:51:35,700 --> 00:51:38,720
The time Holy Father gave us is about
to expire.

363
00:51:40,600 --> 00:51:42,820
May God be with us.

364
00:51:57,900 --> 00:52:01,120
The horse of my father doesn't have a
owner now.

365
00:52:02,500 --> 00:52:05,360
Just like us, it has no one, my son.

366
00:52:06,480 --> 00:52:09,560
They showed no mercy on our mountain-like
Valiant.

367
00:52:11,720 --> 00:52:14,920
Osman Bey promised to get our
revenge, mother.

368
00:52:15,420 --> 00:52:18,000
I believe, he will avenge my father's
death.

369
00:52:33,640 --> 00:52:34,820
Mother!

370
00:52:35,200 --> 00:52:37,760
Just like I told you, he came back!

371
00:52:44,760 --> 00:52:46,380
Welcome, my Bey!

372
00:53:00,020 --> 00:53:01,600
I'm sorry for your loss.

373
00:53:01,660 --> 00:53:03,680
May he rest in heaven.

374
00:53:05,100 --> 00:53:06,460
Thank you, my Bey.

375
00:53:07,060 --> 00:53:11,940
When I heard you summoned him, I prayed
for him to fight against the heathens.

376
00:53:12,660 --> 00:53:15,840
I'm sad because he died before
fighting, my Bey.

377
00:53:17,180 --> 00:53:18,760
My sister.

378
00:53:19,640 --> 00:53:23,600
How lucky you are to be a wife of a
martyr.

379
00:53:26,920 --> 00:53:30,200
Inshallah, you will meet in heaven once
again.

380
00:53:35,280 --> 00:53:39,040
However, Ali promised me something.

381
00:53:40,860 --> 00:53:42,500
He is going to grow up.

382
00:53:45,040 --> 00:53:47,400
And rule his Tent.

383
00:53:48,880 --> 00:53:51,720
After that, we are going to fight side by
side.

384
00:53:52,280 --> 00:53:56,780
And Osman Bey promised that he would
take the revenge of my father's death.

385
00:54:00,880 --> 00:54:02,600
It's already taken, Ali Bey.

386
00:54:12,540 --> 00:54:15,340
With the help of Allah, we became
victorious.

387
00:54:16,640 --> 00:54:18,740
The heathens got defeated harsly.

388
00:54:19,720 --> 00:54:22,120
We made a hill with their heads.

389
00:54:22,740 --> 00:54:26,360
We crushed them so bad that...

390
00:54:28,920 --> 00:54:30,760
Our revenge has been taken.

391
00:54:34,080 --> 00:54:38,380
Inside these chests are the golds we
acquired from the heathens.

392
00:54:38,620 --> 00:54:40,640
They belong to Ali Bey now.

393
00:54:44,600 --> 00:54:46,300
May Allah bless you, my Bey.

394
00:54:46,680 --> 00:54:48,060
May he bless you too.

395
00:54:51,740 --> 00:54:53,820
Bring me the horse of Hasan Bey.

396
00:55:07,860 --> 00:55:09,380
May you saddle it up.

397
00:55:46,160 --> 00:55:47,500
My Ali Bey.

398
00:55:48,540 --> 00:55:50,580
It is entrusted to you now.

399
00:55:52,660 --> 00:55:55,380
Don't you ever worry about your age.

400
00:55:56,560 --> 00:56:02,880
Because, the Sultan of Seljuks, Çağrı
Bey, got sick one day.

401
00:56:03,800 --> 00:56:09,420
And declared his son, Alparslan, a
commander when he was only ten years old.

402
00:56:10,460 --> 00:56:15,020
And our Sultan Alparslan won his first
battle when he was only ten.

403
00:56:17,740 --> 00:56:23,720
My beloved people, our children grow
up with duties and gain foresights.

404
00:56:24,520 --> 00:56:31,600
Because of this, the Bey of this Tent will
be Ali Bey.

405
00:56:38,260 --> 00:56:40,240
You shall all pay homage to him.

406
00:56:43,240 --> 00:56:48,760
From now on, he will be my ears and
eyes in charge of these lands.

407
00:56:52,160 --> 00:56:55,580
He who harms him will harm me too.

408
00:56:57,020 --> 00:57:00,140
His enemies will be my enemies too.

409
00:57:01,920 --> 00:57:05,380
May you all comprehend this well.

410
00:57:09,720 --> 00:57:12,380
I, son of Hasan Gazi, Ali Bey!

411
00:57:13,160 --> 00:57:15,440
From now on, I hold the sword of battles!

412
00:57:15,520 --> 00:57:21,800
Allahu Akbar!

413
00:57:21,920 --> 00:57:29,120
May you live long, Ali Bey!

414
00:58:02,120 --> 00:58:07,720
The hardest part of being a sculptor
is sculpting yourself, Flatyos.

415
00:58:08,760 --> 00:58:15,780
Sculpting yourself is basically
recreating your own-self.

416
00:58:20,060 --> 00:58:21,880
I see you're happy, Nikola.

417
00:58:22,540 --> 00:58:24,160
How can I be not happy?

418
00:58:25,120 --> 00:58:29,160
The emperor made me the lord of
all feudal landlords.

419
00:58:29,260 --> 00:58:31,140
He sent me a new crown.

420
00:58:32,380 --> 00:58:34,120
And my troops are coming.

421
00:58:34,400 --> 00:58:36,000
Of course I'll be happy.

422
00:58:37,920 --> 00:58:41,980
I'm sure you will rule the whole
Rome soon, Nikola.

423
00:58:42,600 --> 00:58:44,320
Don't worry, Flatyos.

424
00:58:45,240 --> 00:58:49,720
When that day comes, you will be
standing next to me.

425
00:58:50,780 --> 00:58:53,360
But first...

426
00:58:54,880 --> 00:58:59,520
... with my new troops, I will make
the Turks...

427
00:59:00,560 --> 00:59:06,520
... regret coming to these lands.

428
00:59:30,400 --> 00:59:37,260
My sir, the support troops got attacked
by Kayıs on their way to İnegöl.

429
00:59:39,360 --> 00:59:41,200
The soldiers are dead.

430
00:59:41,640 --> 00:59:44,620
And Commander Alexander is injured.

431
01:00:09,528 --> 01:00:11,918
Osman...

432
01:00:14,997 --> 01:00:18,997
You...
You...

433
01:00:18,997 --> 01:00:22,997
...you killed my soldiers!

434
01:00:24,003 --> 01:00:29,013
He killed my soldiers!

435
01:00:45,692 --> 01:00:48,122
Osman...

436
01:01:08,942 --> 01:01:12,942
Did he kill my soldiers?

437
01:01:14,656 --> 01:01:20,866
Osman! Did he disband my
unit?

438
01:01:21,348 --> 01:01:27,138
My soldiers, huh?
My unit?

439
01:01:46,095 --> 01:01:51,155
We will fight, Osman. I will
rip you apart.

440
01:01:51,155 --> 01:01:55,875
I will bury every part of you
in a different place.

441
01:01:58,428 --> 01:02:03,008
The beys that you trust so much...

442
01:02:04,408 --> 01:02:08,408
...the alps that you trust so much...

443
01:02:08,408 --> 01:02:12,408
...won't find a piece of you.

444
01:02:12,408 --> 01:02:18,268
I promise you, they won't!

445
01:02:18,268 --> 01:02:22,968
They won't!
They won't!

446
01:02:36,493 --> 01:02:42,743
I promise you! I promise you!
I promise you!

447
01:03:30,995 --> 01:03:34,035
Alps!

448
01:03:34,395 --> 01:03:42,715
Kayı Tribe is under the protection
of Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman Bey.

449
01:04:00,815 --> 01:04:04,815
Ensheathe.

450
01:04:11,131 --> 01:04:14,041
Step forward.

451
01:04:20,341 --> 01:04:21,927
Mashallah.

452
01:04:27,764 --> 01:04:33,684
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

453
01:04:40,203 --> 01:04:45,983
Thank Allah for...

454
01:04:47,924 --> 01:04:51,924
...granting us this victory.

455
01:04:54,649 --> 01:04:56,819
My ghazis...

456
01:04:58,109 --> 01:05:02,949
...ones who deserve it,
should take their shares.

457
01:05:03,642 --> 01:05:08,862
And the people of Kayı should
get their shares too.

458
01:05:11,005 --> 01:05:15,005
My altruistic and valiant mujahids.

459
01:05:15,203 --> 01:05:19,203
From now on...

460
01:05:20,243 --> 01:05:24,243
...we'll run to one battle after another,
one victory after another.

461
01:05:24,243 --> 01:05:28,243
For this reason, we won't relax...

462
01:05:28,243 --> 01:05:32,243
...we won't stop...

463
01:05:32,243 --> 01:05:36,243
...we won't get tired,
we won't run away.

464
01:05:36,243 --> 01:05:40,243
We will always be together.

465
01:05:41,012 --> 01:05:45,832
We'll banish the hypocrites.

466
01:05:46,734 --> 01:05:50,734
And we'll do our job...

467
01:05:50,958 --> 01:05:54,518
...with love.

468
01:05:57,283 --> 01:06:02,633
From now, we will fight...

469
01:06:02,633 --> 01:06:05,553
...and Allah will give
us victory.

470
01:06:05,859 --> 01:06:13,739
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

471
01:06:17,220 --> 01:06:22,980
Alps, hand out the spoils.

472
01:06:47,688 --> 01:06:51,688
Bring my share inside.

473
01:07:03,334 --> 01:07:08,114
What did I tell you?
I told you that Turks are everywhere!

474
01:07:08,961 --> 01:07:15,001
I told you to open your eyes!
I told you to be cautious!

475
01:07:16,269 --> 01:07:21,599
How did they come out of nowhere, Nikola?
They came like ghosts.

476
01:07:21,599 --> 01:07:26,709
We didn't know what to do. All my
soldiers died by their hands.

477
01:07:29,828 --> 01:07:34,948
Alexander, you are an honorable
and a great warrior.

478
01:07:35,734 --> 01:07:39,734
I know this but the thing is...

479
01:07:39,734 --> 01:07:43,734
...being a great warrior...

480
01:07:43,734 --> 01:07:48,974
...isn't enough.
We need more.

481
01:07:50,457 --> 01:07:54,457
You, Flatyos,
invite all the lords...

482
01:07:54,457 --> 01:07:58,457
...that the Emperor gives orders.
I, the lord of lords...

483
01:07:58,457 --> 01:08:02,457
...Nikola, will form a great
crusader army...

484
01:08:02,457 --> 01:08:06,457
...against Turks!

485
01:08:06,457 --> 01:08:12,267
Then, I will behead every Turk
in these lands.

486
01:08:12,267 --> 01:08:17,687
May Allah bless our fallen soldiers.

487
01:10:16,551 --> 01:10:20,271
She is stubborn.
She doesn't milk.

488
01:10:20,271 --> 01:10:24,491
-Maybe you are failing.
-Come and do it then.

489
01:10:24,585 --> 01:10:30,595
-I won't. It's a woman's job.
-Then don't speak as you know it.

490
01:10:32,335 --> 01:10:36,555
What if I do it?
Are you up for a horse race?

491
01:10:56,048 --> 01:11:02,128
-What are you doing, Gonca Hatun?
-You lost on purpose, didn't you?

492
01:11:03,108 --> 01:11:07,238
You did that, Gonca Hatun.

493
01:11:07,653 --> 01:11:11,653
What did I do?

494
01:11:15,599 --> 01:11:21,239
Gonca Hatun, do you really say that you
couldn't milk that goat?

495
01:11:21,776 --> 01:11:25,776
Or did you act to make
me help you?

496
01:11:36,662 --> 01:11:41,482
-How did you know?
-I saw you milking that goat.

497
01:11:41,815 --> 01:11:44,275
When?

498
01:11:46,272 --> 01:11:50,272
I couldn't sleep that night.

499
01:11:51,063 --> 01:11:58,113
Morning's lights were on Ertuğrul
Bey's tent.

500
01:12:01,586 --> 01:12:07,096
-There was hoarfrost, right?
-There was, Gonca Hatun.

501
01:12:08,630 --> 01:12:12,630
And there was a hard
morning frost.

502
01:12:15,269 --> 01:12:21,399
It was so cold. I wanted to
drink milk and get warm.

503
01:12:24,395 --> 01:12:29,895
When I saw you, I couldn't go
anywhere. I was stunned.

504
01:12:32,327 --> 01:12:34,987
Why?

505
01:12:36,901 --> 01:12:40,901
I wanted to get warm.

506
01:12:46,835 --> 01:12:50,035
But...

507
01:12:54,235 --> 01:12:59,635
-But?
-But I didn't want to get burned.

508
01:13:03,122 --> 01:13:06,412
That's what happened.

509
01:13:43,143 --> 01:13:46,913
-Did you control the plates?
-We did, Bala Hatun.

510
01:13:46,913 --> 01:13:48,513
Good.

511
01:13:53,031 --> 01:13:57,871
Bring the bread warm.
Same for the meal.

512
01:13:57,871 --> 01:14:00,141
As you command, Bala Hatun.

513
01:14:02,291 --> 01:14:05,111
More power to you, women!

514
01:14:07,772 --> 01:14:09,982
Gonca.

515
01:14:10,809 --> 01:14:14,809
What's up?
You are smiling.

516
01:14:15,052 --> 01:14:22,622
Bala, finally, Boran Alp has spoken.

517
01:14:24,796 --> 01:14:27,886
My pretty sister.

518
01:14:29,659 --> 01:14:35,349
I'm so glad. Inshallah you will always
be happy.

519
01:14:35,489 --> 01:14:39,489
Inshallah. Thank you, my good sister
Thank you.

520
01:14:41,167 --> 01:14:45,167
You should act quick, Gonca.

521
01:14:45,510 --> 01:14:50,490
Bala, where is Osman Bey?

522
01:14:51,090 --> 01:14:55,090
When will he come?

523
01:14:55,486 --> 01:14:59,486
I wonder that too, Gonca.

524
01:14:59,486 --> 01:15:03,486
After the spoils got shared,
he vanished.

525
01:15:20,126 --> 01:15:24,126
May your victory last forever, Osman Bey.

526
01:15:24,126 --> 01:15:28,126
But I wish you had seen us as well.

527
01:16:21,512 --> 01:16:25,512
Oh my Allah. How much
do you love your Osman that...

528
01:16:25,512 --> 01:16:29,512
...you don't even let me be
mad at him?

529
01:17:13,683 --> 01:17:20,453
-I'm so hungry.
-Come, my child, come. Look!

530
01:17:26,462 --> 01:17:32,782
-Here.
-You told me that my father is an angel.

531
01:17:33,212 --> 01:17:36,440
He must've brought them, right?

532
01:17:36,440 --> 01:17:39,930
It's our state, son.

533
01:17:48,426 --> 01:17:53,796
My Allah, you heard my cryings.
Thak you.

534
01:19:04,485 --> 01:19:08,835
Boran Alp, where is Osman Bey?

535
01:19:12,242 --> 01:19:17,042
I was out of the tribe for something.
Nobody knows.

536
01:19:20,333 --> 01:19:25,713
-Don't you know, Bala Hatun?
-I don't know either, Savcı brother.

537
01:19:33,033 --> 01:19:37,923
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

538
01:19:39,370 --> 01:19:44,730
Mashallah. Our dinner table is
fruitful again.

539
01:20:07,312 --> 01:20:09,592
Go on.

540
01:20:18,025 --> 01:20:23,505
My bey, you were missing.

541
01:20:28,803 --> 01:20:34,293
It's a secret of the bey, Bala.
We can't reveal everything.

542
01:20:40,315 --> 01:20:44,315
With the name of Allah.

543
01:20:46,824 --> 01:20:49,454
Here you go.

544
01:20:51,040 --> 01:20:53,530
With the name of Allah.

545
01:22:42,299 --> 01:22:47,109
-What do you think you are doing?
-Should Cerkutay be hungry?

546
01:22:47,546 --> 01:22:51,546
You can't eat from the boiler!

547
01:22:51,546 --> 01:22:54,096
Did you come down from
a mountain?

548
01:22:57,715 --> 01:23:01,715
Look at me!
Do you know who I am?

549
01:23:03,017 --> 01:23:05,797
Aren't you Aygül?

550
01:23:07,211 --> 01:23:11,211
What are you saying?

551
01:23:14,671 --> 01:23:19,491
You... When did you take it?
Give it back to me!

552
01:23:19,750 --> 01:23:26,240
I'm Cerkutay. I steal things like
this. I don't like to eat what I'm given.

553
01:23:26,240 --> 01:23:29,070
I like to take from other people.

554
01:23:29,285 --> 01:23:33,285
Are you proud of it?

555
01:23:33,498 --> 01:23:37,498
I didn't live in the mountains
but in forests.

556
01:23:39,062 --> 01:23:43,062
I grew up with weasels.

557
01:23:46,648 --> 01:23:49,668
Bear!

558
01:23:52,908 --> 01:23:56,518
Are you mad that I called
you crazy?

559
01:23:57,987 --> 01:24:01,987
If I see you acting like
a weasel again...

560
01:24:02,723 --> 01:24:06,723
...I'll cut your hand.
Remember that.

561
01:24:46,004 --> 01:24:49,554
She is a tough woman.

562
01:25:12,159 --> 01:25:16,709
I congratulate your victory, Osman Bey.
It's a great victory.

563
01:25:16,709 --> 01:25:19,409
It brought glory.

564
01:25:20,893 --> 01:25:27,693
Allah has the real glory.

565
01:25:27,839 --> 01:25:30,679
Allah.

566
01:25:34,101 --> 01:25:37,251
Thank you, uncle.

567
01:25:37,683 --> 01:25:41,683
I congratulate your victory, Osman Bey.
May it last forever.

568
01:25:41,683 --> 01:25:45,683
Thank you too, brother.

569
01:25:45,683 --> 01:25:49,683
-It's because of your good prayers.
-Thank you.

570
01:25:50,041 --> 01:25:54,221
Now, the sword of Jihad is on the
hand of the worthy one.

571
01:25:54,221 --> 01:25:58,221
No one can doubt that.

572
01:26:00,480 --> 01:26:04,480
From now, my brother Savcı is the
scholar and...

573
01:26:04,985 --> 01:26:08,985
...the light of science.

574
01:26:08,985 --> 01:26:11,535
And no one can doubt that.

575
01:26:12,787 --> 01:26:16,787
Thank you, brother.
Thank you.

576
01:26:17,195 --> 01:26:21,195
But without telling you...

577
01:26:21,195 --> 01:26:25,195
...my brother Gündüz and I
started giving lessons for our children.

578
01:26:28,585 --> 01:26:32,585
What a great idea, brother.

579
01:26:32,585 --> 01:26:36,455
No permission is needed for
something so good.

580
01:26:36,455 --> 01:26:41,595
You've done me a favor.
May Allah bless you.

581
01:26:42,235 --> 01:26:45,785
Thank you, brother.

582
01:26:51,743 --> 01:26:55,743
Now, no one can break our unity.

583
01:26:55,743 --> 01:26:59,743
-We should keep our love.
-Amin.

584
01:27:00,244 --> 01:27:04,244
No one can make us forget
that we are brothers...

585
01:27:04,244 --> 01:27:09,444
...that we are of the same blood.

586
01:27:09,646 --> 01:27:12,826
-Amin.
-Amin.

587
01:27:15,710 --> 01:27:18,270
Amin.

588
01:27:35,946 --> 01:27:38,946
Savcı Bey.

589
01:27:40,702 --> 01:27:47,792
-What is the foundation of a state?
-It's family, Osman Bey. Family.

590
01:27:54,482 --> 01:27:59,730
-How can a nation ascend?
-By raising with responsibility...

591
01:27:59,730 --> 01:28:05,550
...morals and honor from the
family.

592
01:28:06,102 --> 01:28:10,782
By learning sharing and helping.

593
01:28:18,793 --> 01:28:24,403
For this reason, family is holy.

594
01:28:24,798 --> 01:28:29,798
Family is sacred.

595
01:28:59,088 --> 01:29:01,568
My brother Boran...

596
01:29:03,928 --> 01:29:07,598
...and my sister Gonca...

597
01:29:08,239 --> 01:29:12,239
...want to marry.

598
01:29:13,080 --> 01:29:16,110
Mashallah. Mashallah.

599
01:29:16,420 --> 01:29:21,580
And I think that it will bring
good.

600
01:29:21,583 --> 01:29:26,643
We should be quick on such
good things.

601
01:29:27,845 --> 01:29:33,475
Now, we'll both fight and
gather a wedding feast!

602
01:30:08,933 --> 01:30:12,023
Boran brother...

603
01:30:12,023 --> 01:30:16,023
...play your qopuz.

604
01:30:17,054 --> 01:30:21,054
-As you order, my bey.
-Thank you.

605
01:30:34,477 --> 01:30:37,667
With the name of Allah.

606
01:30:50,840 --> 01:30:54,840
When you became 20...

607
01:30:55,185 --> 01:30:59,185
...you have seen the dream.

608
01:30:59,821 --> 01:31:03,821
Against the all tyrants...

609
01:31:04,289 --> 01:31:08,289
...Osman Bey stands
like a wall.

610
01:31:08,799 --> 01:31:12,799
Haji Edebali's follower...

611
01:31:13,241 --> 01:31:17,241
...may the towers of the
heathens get demolished.

612
01:31:17,812 --> 01:31:21,812
Ertuğrul Ghazi's pride...

613
01:31:22,512 --> 01:31:26,512
...Osman Bey is a different valiant.

614
01:31:31,420 --> 01:31:35,420
He subdued many people...

615
01:31:38,629 --> 01:31:42,289
...he fought valiantly.

616
01:31:43,422 --> 01:31:47,422
He strikes the tyrants
with his claws...

617
01:31:47,802 --> 01:31:51,802
...Osman Bey is like a
dark wolf.

618
01:31:52,498 --> 01:31:56,498
He strikes the tyrants
with his claws...

619
01:31:57,059 --> 01:32:01,059
...Osman Bey is like a
dark wolf.

620
01:32:19,518 --> 01:32:23,518
On good horses with
grey mane hairs...

621
01:32:24,411 --> 01:32:28,411
...with good armors and
sharp weapons...

622
01:32:29,094 --> 01:32:33,094
...with steel-hearted valiant
alps.

623
01:32:33,345 --> 01:32:37,345
Osman Bey writes a saga.

624
01:32:38,137 --> 01:32:42,137
When the innocents cried...

625
01:32:42,798 --> 01:32:46,798
...the earth shake.

626
01:32:47,282 --> 01:32:51,282
Appeared a hero...

627
01:32:51,988 --> 01:32:55,988
...like a magnificent tent,
Osman Bey.

628
01:33:01,539 --> 01:33:05,539
He subdued many people.

629
01:33:08,398 --> 01:33:12,398
He fought valiantly.

630
01:33:13,490 --> 01:33:17,490
He strikes the tyrants
with his claws.

631
01:33:17,680 --> 01:33:21,680
Osman Bey is like a dark wolf.

632
01:33:22,459 --> 01:33:26,459
He strikes the tyrants
with his claws.

633
01:33:26,854 --> 01:33:30,854
Osman Bey is like a dark wolf.

634
01:35:13,046 --> 01:35:15,886
With the name of Allah.

635
01:35:46,509 --> 01:35:51,649
My bey, what is this salaat
you do?

636
01:35:59,794 --> 01:36:05,024
The salaat we do is gratitude,
Cerkutay.

637
01:36:05,455 --> 01:36:11,895
It's begging. It's remembering
our Allah.

638
01:36:15,270 --> 01:36:19,270
Being in Allah's presence.

639
01:36:20,718 --> 01:36:24,718
We beg to Tengri.

640
01:36:25,974 --> 01:36:29,974
But we don't know Muhammad.

641
01:36:30,518 --> 01:36:33,848
May he rest in peace.

642
01:36:36,182 --> 01:36:42,402
Even Osman Bey turns weird
when he hears that name.

643
01:36:43,776 --> 01:36:46,096
Why is that?

644
01:36:49,438 --> 01:36:55,378
Because Cerkutay, he is the sultan
of both worlds.

645
01:36:55,378 --> 01:36:58,578
Is he so rich?

646
01:37:01,086 --> 01:37:05,086
Some nights, he would sleep
hungry...

647
01:37:05,862 --> 01:37:09,862
...he would repair his own
sweater...

648
01:37:09,862 --> 01:37:15,512
...he would eat a crumble of
betel nut.

649
01:37:18,592 --> 01:37:23,902
Why do you call him a sultan?
He doesn't have anything.

650
01:37:23,902 --> 01:37:29,242
-He can't even solve his hunger.
-Not because he is poor, Cerkutay.

651
01:37:29,425 --> 01:37:33,655
Because of his throne.
His throne.

652
01:37:36,477 --> 01:37:42,897
Cerkutay, the real sultanete
is in the hearts of people.

653
01:37:43,657 --> 01:37:48,307
The real sultan is the one who reigns
in hearts.

654
01:37:51,710 --> 01:37:55,710
And, Cerkutay,
the real conquest...

655
01:37:56,317 --> 01:38:00,317
...is the conquest
of hearts.

656
01:38:00,701 --> 01:38:04,991
That's the kind of sultan he was.

657
01:38:05,711 --> 01:38:11,521
He was merciful,
he was thoughtful...

658
01:38:11,521 --> 01:38:15,521
...he was concerned about his
ummah.

659
01:38:15,744 --> 01:38:22,494
And Cerkutay, he loves children.

660
01:38:28,485 --> 01:38:31,925
Children?

661
01:38:35,476 --> 01:38:38,076
Yes.

662
01:38:42,155 --> 01:38:47,865
Tell me, Cerkutay.
Do you love Muhammad?

663
01:38:50,230 --> 01:38:52,030
I...

664
01:38:54,720 --> 01:38:58,160
Does he love me?

665
01:39:09,735 --> 01:39:14,775
Cerkutay did horrible things.
Cerkutay killed people...

666
01:39:14,775 --> 01:39:18,775
...Cerkutay killed children.

667
01:39:18,775 --> 01:39:22,775
Weasels taught Cerkutay, my bey.
Weasels taught Cerkutay.

668
01:39:24,023 --> 01:39:29,843
Wait, wait, wait.
Hold on, my boy.

669
01:39:29,843 --> 01:39:33,843
Calm down.
Calm down, my son.

670
01:39:33,843 --> 01:39:35,763
Calm down.

671
01:39:42,113 --> 01:39:46,113
My bey, he doesn't love me, does he?

672
01:39:53,293 --> 01:39:56,243
Cerkutay.

673
01:39:56,621 --> 01:40:01,951
We will swear off.
We will beg.

674
01:40:03,549 --> 01:40:07,549
We will cry like this.

675
01:40:07,549 --> 01:40:11,549
We will love children.

676
01:40:11,549 --> 01:40:15,549
We will love women.

677
01:40:15,549 --> 01:40:20,699
We will love trees, the animals.
Everything the god created.

678
01:40:20,699 --> 01:40:25,989
So, he will love us too.

679
01:40:26,557 --> 01:40:32,587
In the other world, he will invite
us to his banner.

680
01:40:35,514 --> 01:40:38,564
Even me?

681
01:40:45,024 --> 01:40:49,024
Even you, Cerkutay.

682
01:40:56,802 --> 01:41:00,332
Even you.

683
01:41:05,722 --> 01:41:09,722
Even you, Cerkutay.

684
01:41:18,920 --> 01:41:24,440
So, what do you think?
How will we improve Söğüt's trade?

685
01:41:28,140 --> 01:41:32,500
From Çobanoğulları
to Germiyanoğulları...

686
01:41:32,944 --> 01:41:37,714
...from Nikea to Prusa,
I have important connections.

687
01:41:39,685 --> 01:41:44,005
If we manage to bring enough
goods to Söğüt...

688
01:41:44,279 --> 01:41:49,739
...after a while, all the merchants
will come here.

689
01:41:50,622 --> 01:41:54,982
Is it easy to bring that much goods,
Dündar Bey?

690
01:41:55,213 --> 01:41:59,213
You know that the road
from Halep to here...

691
01:41:59,213 --> 01:42:02,793
...is very dangerous.

692
01:42:03,178 --> 01:42:08,658
Mongols and bandits are
getting taxes.

693
01:42:10,614 --> 01:42:14,614
What's your solution?

694
01:42:15,012 --> 01:42:20,722
Just like your late father
has done before...

695
01:42:21,626 --> 01:42:25,626
...only you can save
our caravans...

696
01:42:25,626 --> 01:42:29,626
...from them, my bey.

697
01:42:34,122 --> 01:42:40,492
As long as you have such a helper,
I don't doubt how you'll sell your goods.

698
01:42:41,853 --> 01:42:46,513
-He knows what to say.
-Thank you, my bey.

699
01:42:47,713 --> 01:42:51,713
Süleyman is like a son to me.

700
01:42:59,235 --> 01:43:03,235
I've listened to what you've said.

701
01:43:05,023 --> 01:43:09,373
You have my permission
for this.

702
01:43:09,373 --> 01:43:14,743
Kayı alps will protect your caravans.
Your goods will come to Söğüt safely.

703
01:43:18,057 --> 01:43:22,637
Uncle! As a Kayı bey...

704
01:43:22,637 --> 01:43:26,637
...improving the trade
is your duty.

705
01:43:29,579 --> 01:43:34,049
Now their goods are under our
protection...

706
01:43:34,049 --> 01:43:38,804
...if something happens, it's our
duty to pay compensation.

707
01:43:39,068 --> 01:43:40,848
Thank you.

708
01:43:43,464 --> 01:43:45,224
Now...

709
01:43:49,032 --> 01:43:53,962
...my expectation from you is...

710
01:44:02,251 --> 01:44:07,451
When people hear the name Söğüt...

711
01:44:09,625 --> 01:44:15,225
...they'll think of justice, honesty
and security.

712
01:44:16,602 --> 01:44:20,602
Every merchant will think that...

713
01:44:20,602 --> 01:44:23,992
...their goods will be best regarded
in Söğüt.

714
01:44:25,553 --> 01:44:31,113
This is my expectation from you.

715
01:44:36,475 --> 01:44:42,775
-Speak now, uncle.
-If you give me this responsibility...

716
01:44:42,795 --> 01:44:47,035
...I want to revive Söğüt.

717
01:45:00,541 --> 01:45:04,541
We made our first agreement.

718
01:45:10,712 --> 01:45:14,152
May it be good.

719
01:45:16,053 --> 01:45:19,563
May it be good.

720
01:45:19,563 --> 01:45:23,823
Uncle, you will have this duty.

721
01:45:24,071 --> 01:45:28,071
It's your responsibility to revive
Söğüt.

722
01:45:31,103 --> 01:45:36,903
May it be good.
You can talk to each other for the rest.

723
01:45:37,721 --> 01:45:40,001
Thank you.

724
01:45:51,874 --> 01:45:56,184
My bey, it's not my place but...

725
01:45:57,643 --> 01:46:01,643
You wonder if I trust Dündar Bey,
Boran.

726
01:46:03,893 --> 01:46:07,893
My intentions are good.

727
01:46:08,072 --> 01:46:12,072
I gave him another opportunity now.

728
01:46:12,294 --> 01:46:17,794
You should give opportunity and
responsibility to gain their loyalty.

729
01:46:19,908 --> 01:46:22,548
Thank you, my bey.

730
01:46:25,886 --> 01:46:30,186
Form the greatest caravan around here.

731
01:46:30,501 --> 01:46:34,501
I will tell my brother-in-law
Yavlak Arslan too...

732
01:46:34,828 --> 01:46:38,058
...we'll sell goods to Çobanoğlu
market as well.

733
01:46:38,058 --> 01:46:43,468
It'll bring me luck to make business
with a trader like you, Dündar Bey.

734
01:46:43,510 --> 01:46:48,420
We have luck and our way is clear.

735
01:46:48,421 --> 01:46:52,901
Let us begin,
then we'll grow together.

736
01:46:55,622 --> 01:47:01,342
-Come, let us go to my tent.
-Thank you, Dündar Bey.

737
01:47:01,591 --> 01:47:06,491
-We want to visit Bamsı Bey.
-All right.

738
01:47:06,730 --> 01:47:11,950
From now, we are partners.
We'll be seeing each other a lot.

739
01:47:20,526 --> 01:47:24,526
He might've hidden it in his tent.

740
01:47:25,295 --> 01:47:31,445
It seems that it'll be difficult.
We entered Osman's tribe...

741
01:47:31,481 --> 01:47:35,721
...if needed, we'll enter his tent
as well.

742
01:47:35,801 --> 01:47:41,991
-How so?
-Dündar opened the door for us.

743
01:47:43,341 --> 01:47:47,701
Bamsı will take us in.

744
01:47:48,644 --> 01:47:52,644
Let's go and talk to Bamsı Bey...

745
01:47:52,644 --> 01:47:57,114
...about the good old days.

746
01:47:59,939 --> 01:48:04,329
Osman gave you the duty to
keep you on his side.

747
01:48:08,566 --> 01:48:13,976
I'll make him profit a lot, wife.
A lot.

748
01:48:13,976 --> 01:48:17,976
He'll have much more trust
in me.

749
01:48:17,976 --> 01:48:22,386
He'll love his uncle a lot.

750
01:48:22,989 --> 01:48:29,359
I'll strangle him with the
bow string he used.

751
01:48:29,530 --> 01:48:36,120
He'll ask for mercy,
he'll ask me to forgive him.

752
01:48:40,062 --> 01:48:44,592
That day, you won't forgive him,
Dündar Bey.

753
01:48:45,423 --> 01:48:51,153
His annoying wife gave orders
to everyone today.

754
01:48:51,966 --> 01:48:56,996
She gave me, the only daughter
of Çobanoğullar...

755
01:48:57,585 --> 01:49:00,955
...an order.

756
01:49:01,529 --> 01:49:07,679
That moment, I felt like I was under
a boulder.

757
01:49:09,304 --> 01:49:13,304
Just for you...

758
01:49:13,974 --> 01:49:20,884
...I was patient. Just for you.

759
01:49:22,501 --> 01:49:26,501
My beautiful wife.

760
01:49:27,452 --> 01:49:32,382
Stay calm.
Stay calm.

761
01:49:32,627 --> 01:49:37,697
We'll ask them for what they've
done to us.

762
01:49:37,898 --> 01:49:41,898
-Inshallah.
-We will.

763
01:49:43,877 --> 01:49:48,077
-May I enter, Dündar Bey?
-Brother?

764
01:49:52,352 --> 01:49:56,352
Come, Yavlak Arslan.

765
01:49:57,322 --> 01:50:01,322
-Brother!
-Sister.

766
01:50:03,170 --> 01:50:06,370
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

767
01:50:06,370 --> 01:50:08,850
Alaikum Salam.

768
01:50:09,553 --> 01:50:15,483
What's wrong, Yavlak Arslan?
What brought you here at night?

769
01:50:15,835 --> 01:50:21,045
I was hunting at night.
A gazelle brought me here.

770
01:50:21,182 --> 01:50:26,232
Sertaç warned me to not enter
Osman's tents but...

771
01:50:28,401 --> 01:50:33,231
...I wanted to see my sister.
-Welcome, brother. Welcome.

772
01:50:33,467 --> 01:50:39,197
Come. Not at all. This is your
tent as well.

773
01:50:44,095 --> 01:50:49,025
So, it's been a long while.
Osman became a bey.

774
01:50:49,122 --> 01:50:53,482
And you lost all your duties, is that so?

775
01:50:54,116 --> 01:50:58,726
Yes, but you...

776
01:50:59,760 --> 01:51:06,290
...became Osman's ally.
-Yes, I have.

777
01:51:10,611 --> 01:51:13,911
Thank you.

778
01:51:19,556 --> 01:51:23,556
How did you do that, brother?

779
01:51:26,505 --> 01:51:31,455
Osman Bey is shrewd, a good warrior...

780
01:51:31,455 --> 01:51:38,095
...he is a smart man. Only he could
watch my back against Geyhatu.

781
01:51:39,241 --> 01:51:44,841
He should stop Byzantine here
and I will kick Geyhatu out of here.

782
01:51:46,074 --> 01:51:53,184
These lands will be the home of
Islam and Turks again.

783
01:51:53,546 --> 01:51:58,046
-Inshallah.
-Inshallah.

784
01:51:58,227 --> 01:52:03,487
Brother, you should stay here tonight.
Be our guest.

785
01:52:04,963 --> 01:52:08,963
The night is long.
We can talk.

786
01:52:10,289 --> 01:52:15,419
We have things to tell you
as well.

787
01:54:28,461 --> 01:54:31,831
My bey, what is this?

788
01:54:34,939 --> 01:54:38,829
It's our flag.

789
01:54:39,273 --> 01:54:42,393
A new flag?

790
01:54:49,017 --> 01:54:53,307
-Wouldn't the beys object?
-They wouldn't.

791
01:54:55,902 --> 01:54:59,902
They won't.

792
01:55:01,864 --> 01:55:05,864
Because...

793
01:55:06,131 --> 01:55:09,941
...this flag has a meaning...

794
01:55:11,220 --> 01:55:15,220
...it's for the Islam world.

795
01:55:15,580 --> 01:55:21,750
Inshallah, we'll be the hope of
the whole Islam world.

796
01:55:22,006 --> 01:55:24,786
Inshallah.

797
01:55:26,386 --> 01:55:33,266
From a tribe to beylic, and
from there to the whole world...

798
01:55:34,074 --> 01:55:37,414
...we will spread out.

799
01:55:43,160 --> 01:55:45,820
Bala.

800
01:55:46,824 --> 01:55:50,994
-Give this to the women.
-As you order, my bey.

801
01:56:19,669 --> 01:56:25,599
My bey, you handed out your
share, didn't you?

802
01:56:29,403 --> 01:56:33,403
Thank Allah.
Thank Allah.

803
01:56:35,089 --> 01:56:41,129
-No one knows, right?
-What did our prophet say?

804
01:56:43,403 --> 01:56:48,183
One hand shouldn't see the other's
charity.

805
01:56:50,487 --> 01:56:55,537
When it's seen by people, it's not charity
but tyranny to the one taking the help.

806
01:56:58,342 --> 01:57:04,352
And since I'm the bey, it's
my responsibility.

807
01:57:05,302 --> 01:57:08,712
Mashallah, my bey.

808
01:57:23,213 --> 01:57:25,463
Bala.

809
01:57:25,689 --> 01:57:30,119
-Yes, my bey.
-I love your pretty eyes.

810
02:00:57,781 --> 02:01:00,561
Father!

811
02:01:01,519 --> 02:01:03,919
Son.

812
02:01:13,276 --> 02:01:15,826
My will.

813
02:01:59,991 --> 02:02:03,601
My will, Osman.

814
02:02:07,038 --> 02:02:10,318
My will.

815
02:03:34,610 --> 02:03:38,610
My will, Osman.
My will.

816
02:04:16,195 --> 02:04:18,875
Father...

817
02:06:04,545 --> 02:06:07,115
Osman?

818
02:06:13,332 --> 02:06:15,642
Bala...

819
02:06:42,887 --> 02:06:45,197
My father...

820
02:06:46,855 --> 02:06:50,855
...left a will before dying.

821
02:07:05,903 --> 02:07:09,903
He wants me to have a new wife.

822
02:07:24,207 --> 02:07:28,207
It's my father's will.

823
02:07:28,499 --> 02:07:32,139
I will do it.

824
02:07:36,014 --> 02:07:39,864
I will have a new wife.

825
02:07:42,121 --> 02:07:45,521
It's true now.

826
02:07:48,132 --> 02:07:51,852
I wanted you to know.

827
02:08:03,553 --> 02:08:07,553
Horsefeathers to you, Osman.

828
02:08:11,848 --> 02:08:17,448
Why didn't you tell me all this time?

829
02:08:36,837 --> 02:08:41,717
I couldn't hit a gazelle like you,
looking directly into your eyes.

830
02:08:45,959 --> 02:08:49,959
Not at all, Osman.

831
02:08:56,999 --> 02:09:02,339
Haven't I told you to have
a new wife?

832
02:09:09,958 --> 02:09:14,368
See, our Ertuğrul Bey ordered it.

833
02:09:15,215 --> 02:09:20,725
There is no return now.
It's your father's will.

834
02:09:20,998 --> 02:09:24,598
It's your bey's will.

835
02:09:28,421 --> 02:09:32,421
You will do it.

836
02:09:39,802 --> 02:09:43,802
Don't cry.

837
02:09:48,568 --> 02:09:52,568
No, Osman.

838
02:09:55,692 --> 02:09:59,872
If you cry, you will make us suffer.

839
02:10:04,404 --> 02:10:07,194
I won't cry.

840
02:10:09,233 --> 02:10:14,973
I won't rebel. I'll be patient.

841
02:10:27,374 --> 02:10:31,374
This is our fate, Osman.

842
02:10:32,047 --> 02:10:35,667
This is our fate.

843
02:13:43,567 --> 02:13:47,567
O' the throne!

844
02:13:50,590 --> 02:13:54,590
What do you want from me?

845
02:14:01,894 --> 02:14:05,894
How hard is it to sit on you?

846
02:14:12,509 --> 02:14:16,509
O' the throne!

847
02:14:17,468 --> 02:14:21,468
You don't accept two beys on you.

848
02:14:22,232 --> 02:14:26,232
You don't share me with
anyone.

849
02:14:27,654 --> 02:14:33,073
O' the fur, you say the future of Kayı...

850
02:14:34,914 --> 02:14:40,814
...but you make me threaten...

851
02:14:42,049 --> 02:14:46,049
...even my most beloved ones.

852
02:14:52,993 --> 02:14:56,993
O' the throne!

853
02:14:57,096 --> 02:15:02,126
You say the stability,
the future...

854
02:15:02,737 --> 02:15:05,747
...children...

855
02:15:06,636 --> 02:15:10,636
...but...

856
02:15:13,282 --> 02:15:16,702
...but...

857
02:15:21,138 --> 02:15:24,148
...you give sorrow to...

858
02:15:26,031 --> 02:15:29,461
...the person...

859
02:15:39,846 --> 02:15:43,846
...I love the most.

860
02:15:51,379 --> 02:15:54,959
My heart and soul...

861
02:15:55,420 --> 02:15:58,470
...my love.

862
02:15:59,908 --> 02:16:05,388
You throw her to dungeons...

863
02:16:07,105 --> 02:16:11,105
...with my hands and words.

864
02:16:49,625 --> 02:16:52,905
My Allah...

865
02:16:54,335 --> 02:16:57,316
...don't leave me alone.

866
02:16:58,885 --> 02:17:04,645
Don't leave me alone, my Allah.
On this difficult mission...

867
02:17:07,989 --> 02:17:12,779
...don't make me one of those
who lost their ways.

868
02:17:14,627 --> 02:17:21,087
Keep me on our prophet's
path always.

869
02:17:23,221 --> 02:17:27,221
Give me true friends.

870
02:17:27,412 --> 02:17:33,632
Keep me on your path always.

871
02:17:36,061 --> 02:17:39,370
Keep me.

872
02:17:50,731 --> 02:17:54,731
Osman Bey!
May I enter?

873
02:17:55,689 --> 02:17:58,648
Come in.

874
02:18:34,793 --> 02:18:39,913
They said that Osman Bey ascended
to the throne, so I came with a gift.

875
02:18:44,082 --> 02:18:49,201
But it seems, the throne is
on the shoulders of Osman Bey.

876
02:18:52,254 --> 02:18:56,254
My burden is heavy.

877
02:18:57,727 --> 02:19:02,718
-What is its secret?
-You shouldn't ask me...

878
02:19:03,520 --> 02:19:08,360
...but to this wood that turned
into this shape, bey's son.

879
02:19:22,906 --> 02:19:26,906
Forgive me, Osman Bey.

880
02:19:29,206 --> 02:19:34,476
-You honored my tent.
-Not at all.

881
02:19:35,373 --> 02:19:38,173
Not at all.

882
02:19:42,084 --> 02:19:45,263
Come.

883
02:19:48,953 --> 02:19:52,263
With the name of Allah.

884
02:19:55,987 --> 02:19:59,987
It's very huge.

885
02:20:00,772 --> 02:20:04,772
Thank Allah. Thank Allah.

886
02:20:05,571 --> 02:20:09,571
Thank Allah, Osman Bey.
Thank Allah.

887
02:20:09,868 --> 02:20:14,998
How many people can have
such a big tent nowadays?

888
02:20:23,763 --> 02:20:29,263
If you accept it...

889
02:20:29,388 --> 02:20:33,238
...I want to give you a gift,
Osman Bey.

890
02:20:55,802 --> 02:20:59,802
It's a dervish accessory.
You put it on your neck.

891
02:21:02,081 --> 02:21:06,081
Give it to me.
Like this.

892
02:21:21,511 --> 02:21:24,111
What does it do?

893
02:21:24,343 --> 02:21:28,343
To beg, Osman Bey.
To beg.

894
02:21:29,610 --> 02:21:33,610
Dervish doesn't ask for from anyone
but Allah.

895
02:21:34,888 --> 02:21:39,988
But this two-headed dragon...
Our desires...

896
02:21:40,224 --> 02:21:45,204
Dervishes wear this to tame
their desires.

897
02:21:45,455 --> 02:21:49,455
And go into life...

898
02:21:49,459 --> 02:21:53,459
...and you start to
travel the world.

899
02:21:53,459 --> 02:21:57,459
The people once you had to compete
for the earthly goods, laugh at you.

900
02:21:57,459 --> 02:22:01,459
They pity you.

901
02:22:01,459 --> 02:22:05,459
And every laugh is cost you.
Some leave a gold...

902
02:22:05,459 --> 02:22:09,459
...some leave food.

903
02:22:10,829 --> 02:22:14,829
Some leave trash.

904
02:22:17,172 --> 02:22:21,172
Every day, every gold...

905
02:22:21,172 --> 02:22:25,172
...destroys the idol that you
built with your desires.

906
02:22:25,172 --> 02:22:31,472
The days pass and this becomes
your closest friend.

907
02:22:32,932 --> 02:22:36,932
And when you destroy your
idols...

908
02:22:36,932 --> 02:22:40,932
...this becomes your crown.

909
02:22:40,932 --> 02:22:46,012
You start to see the world
with different eyes.

910
02:22:48,144 --> 02:22:52,144
Then, the world shows you
its secrets.

911
02:22:59,079 --> 02:23:01,629
Osman Bey.

912
02:23:02,558 --> 02:23:06,558
Osman the Dark, the hope of...

913
02:23:06,558 --> 02:23:11,688
...all Turkmens, the Islam world...

914
02:23:11,688 --> 02:23:16,548
...mothers, fathers, sons, daughters
even children, and dervishes!

915
02:23:17,175 --> 02:23:19,975
Not at all.

916
02:23:21,794 --> 02:23:26,344
This has been my comrade
for years.

917
02:23:27,075 --> 02:23:30,985
Now it's yours.

918
02:23:57,799 --> 02:24:01,799
You are a great bey.

919
02:24:01,799 --> 02:24:06,809
Don't say that what will I do with it.
It's a metaphor. Understand it.

920
02:24:08,675 --> 02:24:12,675
If you want to demolish the idol
that says...

921
02:24:12,675 --> 02:24:17,865
... ''I'm a bey, I know everything''
you should beg like a dervish.

922
02:24:25,256 --> 02:24:29,256
What will I beg for?

923
02:24:53,099 --> 02:24:57,339
The thing that makes you a bey.

924
02:24:59,024 --> 02:25:03,514
You should beg for knowledge
from the experts.

925
02:25:04,360 --> 02:25:10,100
You should gather all those
who know, in this tent.

926
02:25:10,100 --> 02:25:14,100
You should leave everything to
the one who know it.

927
02:25:14,100 --> 02:25:19,170
Best scholars, talented artists,
good warriors...

928
02:25:19,170 --> 02:25:23,170
...should gather in this tent.

929
02:25:26,213 --> 02:25:28,473
Osman Bey.

930
02:25:32,119 --> 02:25:36,119
Bey! You are a bey now.

931
02:25:36,239 --> 02:25:40,239
The wolf on the mountain,
the sheep in the herd...

932
02:25:40,239 --> 02:25:45,019
...the wind that blows, the bird
in the sky are under your protection.

933
02:25:45,226 --> 02:25:49,886
How can you be strong enough?
How can you have that much time?

934
02:25:49,886 --> 02:25:54,996
The knowledge that you
save in this...

935
02:25:54,996 --> 02:25:59,126
...the people you save in this
will solve your problems.

936
02:26:01,795 --> 02:26:06,895
Then, this throne won't
be on your shoulders.

937
02:26:07,066 --> 02:26:11,476
You will sit on it.

938
02:26:11,709 --> 02:26:15,839
Then, this tent will be the
center of the world.

939
02:26:15,839 --> 02:26:19,839
And it will bring justice to
all living.

940
02:26:21,135 --> 02:26:26,215
And your lineage will be known
as Osmans (Ottomans).

941
02:26:31,219 --> 02:26:38,579
Osmans (Ottomans).

942
02:26:39,421 --> 02:26:44,631
Ottomans! Ottomans!

943
02:26:44,631 --> 02:26:50,831
Ottomans!
Ottomans!

944
02:26:51,930 --> 02:26:55,470
Allahu Akbar!

945
02:27:14,512 --> 02:27:35,517
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com